+# Research
+
+## Request path
+
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/category/CategoryApi.java` maps `DELETE /api/v1/private/category/{id}` to `CategoryFacade.deleteCategory`.
+- `CategoryFacadeImpl.deleteCategory(Long, MerchantStore)` currently resolves the category with `categoryService.getById(categoryId)` and delegates to `CategoryService.delete`.
+- `CategoryFacadeImpl.getById` already raises `ResourceNotFoundException` when the category lookup returns null. The delete lookup should likewise be store-scoped and must not silently accept a missing category.
+
+## Current cause
+
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/catalog/category/CategoryServiceImpl.java` builds the deleted category's subtree from its lineage, finds products in those category ids, and then:
+  - calls `productService.delete(dbProduct)` when a product has only one category, which removes the product and its inventory/price relationships;
+  - removes category references and updates only products with more than one category;
+  - deletes only the root category afterward, relying on `Category.categories` (`cascade = CascadeType.REMOVE`) for descendants.
+- This explains missing products, broken carts, and broken order loading. `ShoppingCartItem` stores `productId` and `sku`, and `OrderProduct` stores the order-line `sku` and snapshot fields; neither needs category rows to exist. Deleting the product itself is therefore the damaging operation.
+- Product/category membership is a `@ManyToMany` association in `sm-core-model/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/model/catalog/product/Product.java`, backed by `PRODUCT_CATEGORY`. Removing the category from each affected product and saving the product must happen before category rows are deleted.
+- `Category` in `sm-core-model/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/model/catalog/category/Category.java` has `@OneToMany(mappedBy = "parent", cascade = CascadeType.REMOVE)` for descendants and cascading descriptions. The implementation must remove all subtree category references from products, then delete the subtree categories without deleting products.
+
+## Other affected behavior
+
+- Product filtering in `ProductRepositoryImpl.getProductsListByCategories` joins `p.categories`, so after the mapping rows are removed `GET /api/v1/products?category={id}` naturally returns no products for deleted category ids.
+- Product detail/category mapping uses `Product.categories`; after the mapping cleanup, `GET /api/v2/product/{sku}` will retain product data but no longer expose deleted categories.
+- Category hierarchy and id lookups use `CategoryRepository` queries and the facade's `ResourceNotFoundException`; once the category rows are deleted, GET by id and hierarchy listing will omit them / return 404.
+- Existing code does not annotate the category delete operation transactional. The implementation should make the product mapping cleanup and category deletion one transaction so a failed delete cannot leave partial associations.
+
+## Test coverage reviewed
+
+- `sm-shop/src/test/java/com/salesmanager/test/shop/integration/category/CategoryManagementAPIIntegrationTest.java` covers basic category reads/creation but does not cover deletion semantics.
+- `sm-core/src/test/java/com/salesmanager/test/catalog/CategoryTest.java` only tests category creation/read and cleanup.
+- The relevant regression should exercise a product with only the deleted category, a product with another surviving category too, a child category, and a missing delete id; it should verify product retention, category mappings, category/product listing, and 404 behavior.
